------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scientific and technical sources
------------------------------------------------------------------------
HAZEL's calculation engine is an independent implementation, written from the
following published sources. The source of each formula is cited in the code
next to it. These works are credited here; no text or code from them is
redistributed except for short quotations, marked as such in code comments.

- NOAA / EPA, "ALOHA 5.4.4 Technical Documentation", NOAA Technical
  Memorandum NOS OR&R 43 (2013). The formulas follow this document; the
  side-by-side comparison runs described on the About page were made with the
  ALOHA program, version 5.4.7.
- Spicer, T. O. and Havens, J. A., "User's Guide for the DEGADIS 2.1 Dense Gas
  Dispersion Model", US EPA, EPA-450/4-89-019 (1989).
- Havens, J. A. and Spicer, T. O., "Development of an Atmospheric Dispersion
  Model for Heavier-than-Air Gas Mixtures", Volume I (1985), Defense Technical
  Information Center, ADA171522.
- Chamberlain, G. A., "Development in Design Methods for Predicting Thermal
  Radiation from Flares", Chemical Engineering Research and Design 65,
  299-309 (1987).
- The further primary literature cited in the source files and on the About
  page, including Pasquill (1961), Briggs (1973), Beals (1971), Palazzi et al.
  (1982), Mudan (1984), Roberts (1982), Moorhouse and Pritchard (1982),
  Sherman (1980), Wilson (1987), and the AIChE guidelines for vapour cloud
  explosion evaluation (1994).

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data
------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Chemical data (data/chemicals.json, data/chemicals.slim.json): derived from the US
  Department of Energy "Protective Action Criteria (PAC) with AEGLs, ERPGs and
  TEELs" dataset, a work of the US Government. Conversion script:
  tools/convert_pac_data.py.
- Map data and tiles: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open
  Database Licence (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright). Tiles are
  fetched from the OpenStreetMap tile servers, subject to their tile usage
  policy.
- Weather data (only when an operator configures a relay): MET Norway,
  Locationforecast, licensed CC BY 4.0 / NLOD 2.0
  (https://api.met.no/). The attribution text shown in the application must
  not be removed when this feature is enabled.

